    {
      "evidenceId": "evidence:waage",
      "text": "Only a ring of straw is left on the fair scale. Its log: 14:05 “Otto”, 312 kilos, record. 15:00:00 weight drops to zero. Otto did not leave on his own.",
      "mentions": [
        {
          "kind": "location",
          "id": "location:wiegezelt"
        },
        {
          "kind": "item",
          "id": "item:kuerbis"
        }
      ],
      "reports": []
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "evidence:handschuhe",
      "text": "Next to the scale lie flowery gardening gloves, embroidered: H. M. Everyone in the village knows them, Hilde Moosbrugger has worn them for twenty years. When they were left here, they do not tell.",
      "mentions": [
        {
          "kind": "person",
          "id": "person:hilde"
        },
        {
          "kind": "location",
          "id": "location:wiegezelt"
        }
      ],
      "reports": []
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "evidence:schleifspur",
      "text": "Behind the tent the canvas is rolled up. A broad, flattened trail leads through the grass right across the fairground to the car park meadow. Something very round and very heavy was rolled here.",
      "mentions": [
        {
          "kind": "location",
          "id": "location:parkwiese"
        }
      ],
      "reports": []
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "evidence:parkschein",
      "text": "In the car park meadow stands a ladder wagon with fresh straw and a broken-off pumpkin leaf. A parking ticket for the fair meadow is clipped to the wagon: “Entry 14:40, F. Kranz, Oberbrunn.” So Ferdinand Kranz was at the fair today.",
      "mentions": [
        {
          "kind": "person",
          "id": "person:ferdl"
        },
        {
          "kind": "location",
          "id": "location:parkwiese"
        },
